+The segmenter lays out verse itself: each source line stays whole, the first sits on the verse's
+first Pali row, equal counts take one on each, and unequal counts use as many rows as there are
+whole lines to fill them. A speaker label stays with its speech. `report.json`'s `verseLayouts`
+lists the layouts applied, declined, or kept because a review settled them; a review always wins.
+For a new or revised text, readers check unequal-count grouping or gap placement against the Pali,
+and settle verse ownership where a source line crosses a verse boundary or interleaves its
+neighbours. Printed prose, abbreviations and other places with no source breaks stay for the
+ordinary cuts/read-through rounds.
